the prosecution have been taking the  jury through the events of the hours  that led up to the death of dalian  atkinson who was of course  a well-known professional footballer  best known for playing  for aston villa now they were told that  it was  in the early hours of the morning back  in august uh in 2016 that mr atkinson's  behavior  on that night had been both distressed  and erratic and he was banging on the  door of his father's home  in telford demanding to be let in now  now neighbors had  seen what was happening and had been  alarmed and they called the police  and the police officers that attended  were pc  benjamin monk and pc marielle and betley  smith  both both from west mercier police  now pc monk had a taser and there were a  number of  confrontations uh when they knocked on  that door and daley and atkinson  answered we're told mr atkinson was  unarmed but pc monk deployed his taser  three times now the first two times that  he deployed it it was the jury  we're told ineffective it appeared to  have no effect on mr atkinson but the  third time that he deployed the taser  we're told it was completely effective  daley and atkinson fell  face first into the road and was  according to neighbors who  were watching what happened completely  unresponsive now the jury were told that  the normal cycle of a taser is  five seconds but that the taser user can  override that  by continuing to press the trigger and  that in this case pc monk did override  it  in fact the taser was deployed for some  33 seconds more than six times  longer than would be usual and then the  jury were told that pc monk  uh once stalin atkinson was on the  ground kicked him  twice in the head so hard that the  imprint of the police constables boot  laces was seen  on two parts of mr atkinson's forehead  we're told pc betley smith used her bat  on also to strike mr atkinson  while he was on the ground and the jury  were told that  pc monk was an experienced officer but  that he must have been  angry um that he was in this situation  and in kicking dalian atkinson to the  head he can only have intended  to cause really serious harm now by the  time  the ambulance arrived dalian atkinson  was unconscious by the time he got to  hospital  he was in cardiac arrest and he died a  short time later  the prosecutor said that she had taken  evidence from a  specialist a pathologist and specialist  in intensive care  whose opinion it was that were it not  for the extended third taser or the  kicks to the head  daily and atkinson would not have died  that night  now that is uh the jury we're told in  spite of the fact that mr atkinson was  suffering some health conditions at the  time he was in renal failure  and did have some heart disease now pc  monk  denies the murder charge and the  alternate charge of manslaughter against  him and pc betley smith denies assault  the trial is expected to last some six  to eight weeks
 

